# Files a Linux shell or daemon reads have to keep LF endings whatever core.autocrlf does
# on the machine that checked them out. A CRLF shebang fails with a "bad interpreter"
# error that names an invisible character, and the cloud-init template carries shell
# scripts inside it that would inherit the same problem on the droplet's first boot.
*.sh      text eol=lf
*.tftpl   text eol=lf
Caddyfile text eol=lf

# The PubquizR corpus is compared byte for byte by cmd/quizfmt/encode_test.go, so a CRLF
# working copy fails that test locally while CI passes. Every file is already LF in the index.
src/playhaus-api/internal/pubquizr/data/**/*.json text eol=lf
